---
title: "deposit_collateral - Deposit Collateral to Obligation (Scallop Lend)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_version: check version == current_version
    q_check_version --> q_error_version: version mismatch
    q_error_version --> [*]: abort error
    q_check_version --> q_check_lock: version matches
    q_check_lock --> q_error_locked: obligation is locked (staked in borrow incentive)
    q_error_locked --> [*]: abort 770
    q_check_lock --> q_check_active: obligation not locked
    q_check_active --> q_error_inactive: collateral type not active
    q_error_inactive --> [*]: abort 73730
    q_check_active --> q_check_type: collateral type active
    q_check_type --> q_error_type: invalid collateral type
    q_error_type --> [*]: abort 1794
    q_check_type --> q_check_same_asset: valid collateral type
    q_check_same_asset --> q_error_same: coin type == borrowed coin type
    q_error_same --> [*]: abort 1796
    q_check_same_asset --> q_check_cap: coin type != borrowed coin type
    q_check_cap --> q_error_cap: collateral_total >= collateral_capacity
    q_error_cap --> [*]: abort error
    q_check_cap --> q_deposit: collateral_total < collateral_capacity
    q_deposit --> q_update: obligation.collaterals[T] += coin_value
    q_update --> [*]: emit CollateralDepositEvent

    note right of q_deposit
        INV-001: anyone can deposit collateral into any obligation (no ObligationKey required)
        INV-002: collateral amount increases by exactly coin_value
        INV-003: cannot deposit same coin type as already-borrowed coin type in same obligation
        INV-004: collateral_total <= collateral_capacity for each asset
    end note
